G|0|0|0|0|1|Parity ok (discrepancy_first lean: 1 excerpt vs discrepancy's named-skeptic connective, 1>=1). Connectives accurate on both poles, no overclaim. Baur real & fairly represented: Paulus, der Apostel Jesu Christi (1845) is his authenticated work; Tübingen School's central case against common authorship of 1/2 Thess was precisely this imminence-vs-staged-signs eschatological contradiction (verified via web search). Haley pd_work verified real and on-topic — archive.org examinationof00hale pp.134-135 carry the exact "His coming at hand. / It was far off." two-column table, quote De Wette, Davidson, and Andrew Fuller verbatim, then conclude "this 'discrepancy' of which Baur makes so much, really amounts to nothing" (all confirmed verbatim). BUT the note's specific citation is wrong: Haley's table cites 1 Cor 15:51-52, Phil 4:5, 1 Thess 4:15, and 1 Pet iv. 7 against 2 Thess 2:2-3 — there is no "2 Pet 3:7-9" anywhere near this discussion (checked full "Peter"/"2 Pet" search hits, none fall on pp.148-153), and "1 Thess 4:15-17/5:1-3" overstates what's actually tabulated (only 4:15). Fabricated/incorrect verse detail inside an otherwise accurate note -> flag, not missing.
